💡 **SUGGESTION: the `(connect watchdog)` classifier couples to a display string produced in another module**

This pattern matches the human-readable wording emitted by `watchdogTimedOut()` in `provider_common.dart` (`… no response headers within ${…}s (connect watchdog)`). If that message is ever reworded, the #1125 ladder-exhaustion classification silently reverts to the pre-#1121 behavior (dies as a raw error).

The producer side is already test-pinned (`connect_stall_retry_test.dart` asserts `contains('(connect watchdog)')`), so drift would be caught by CI — but both files live in `lib/src/providers/`, so a shared constant makes the contract structural instead of incidental:

```dart
// provider_common.dart
const String connectWatchdogTag = '(connect watchdog)';

// transient_retry_stream.dart
RegExp(RegExp.escape(connectWatchdogTag)),
